-- Backfill Zimbabwe downscaled crop water requirements and missing crop_data master rows.
-- Districts: Mangwe, Mwenezi, Chipinge, Rushinga. Masvingo already exists and is left as-is.
--
-- Part 1 inserts missing zw crop_data master rows: the dashboard probability table
-- (generateTable) drops any crop/variety with no matching crop_data row, which is why
-- only varieties already present (e.g. NATAL-COMMON, CBC-2, IT-18) rendered.
-- Days come from the extractor modal ranges (Rushinga direct from doc table);
-- maturity_period follows existing per-crop bands; additional_info is source district.
--
-- Part 2 upserts the downscaled water requirements. Crop keys are normalised to the
-- master taxonomy (pearl-millet/finger-millet -> millet, sugar-beans -> beans,
-- ground-nuts -> groundnuts, p/millet -> millet). Station links:
--   Mangwe -> Plumtree (zw/plumtree_met), Mwenezi -> Buffalo Range (zw/buffalo_range_met),
--   Chipinge -> Chisumbanje (zw/chisumbanje_met), Rushinga -> Mount Darwin (zw/mt_darwin,
--   doc notes Mt Darwin data is wetter than most of Rushinga).
-- Upserts on generated ids, safe to re-run.


-- Ensure referenced climate stations exist before inserting downscaled rows
-- (guarantees foreign key constraint succeeds during clean local resets without altering remote data)
on conflict (country_code, station_id) do nothing;

